WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
Mason turns one real PCB into two types of solder-paste printing tools.

00:04.000 --> 00:09.000
PCB2 is 85 × 60 mm, with 347 parsed top-paste pads and 106 bottom-paste pads.

00:09.000 --> 00:14.000
Use a jig with a metal stencil, or print a standalone PCB stencil for prototyping.

00:14.000 --> 00:17.000
Top to bottom: A-side cover, metal stencil, B-side base, PCB tray.

00:17.000 --> 00:19.200
Clamp the metal stencil between the cover and base using the perimeter screws.

00:19.200 --> 00:23.000
Lower the complete assembly onto the tray's four alignment posts. The corner posts are not screws.

00:23.000 --> 00:28.000
Check the model, then export STL / STEP. Download the same Gerber example from the website.
